Seeks to ensure that the plea bargaining procedure is not exploited as a means 
of compromise for the convenience of the guilty.

Provides for several principles which shall be considered when plea bargaining agreement shall be entered into by and between the prosecution and the accused:  
a) it shall be imbued with public interest;
b) it shall be based on the premise that the interest of justice and of the public will be served;
c) it shall not be a matter of compromise or of right but shall be addressed to the sound discretion of the trial court;
d) it shall not be entered into when it will only serve to trivialize the seriousness of the offense nor negate the deterrent value of the law.

Provides for the appropriate lesser offense and its corresponding penalty;
the offended party whose consent is necessary; offended parties in case of plunder and money laundering; the time and conditions avail; and the procedures to be followed.

Seeks to ensure that information or access to all available scholarships and other programs and
incentives initiated by the government or other private institutions are made accessible to the widest possible recipients.

Enumerates the duties and functions of the National Scholarship Commission as regards to the following:
a) comprehensive database of OSCY and other qualified individuals nationwide;
b) issues and/or controversies that are keeping children and youth out of schools and formal
education;
c) information and/or data that could help them get back to formal education;
d) existing regular and/or special scholarships/educational grants; and
e) the necessary procedures and/or processes as regards the scholarships/grants.

States that an amount of Ten Thousand Pesos (P10,000.00) per month shall be granted as additional compensation to the existing salary and benefits of the concerned Educators which shall be paid in three (3) tranches, as follows:
First Year - P4,000.00 per month;
Second Year - additional P3,000.00 per month
Third Year - another additional of P3,000.00 per month.

Provides for authorized additional support as follows:
a.Support in the form of allowances and other remuneration funded from 
local school board funds;
b.Medical allowance for medical check-up in the amount of One Thousand 
Pesos (P1,000.00) per year;
c.Annual Magna Carta bonus which shall be equivalent to the entitlement under RA 4670.

Defines the terms \"Take Home Pay\" and \"Authorized Deductions\".

Provides that the minimum monthly take home pay of all government employees after all the authorized deductions shall be at all times thirty percent (30%) of their monthly salary.

Prioritizes the authorized deductions in the following order:
a. BIR, GSIS, HDMF, and the PHIC;
b. Mutual benefit associations, thrift banks, and non-stock savings and loan associations;
c. Associations or Cooperatives;
d. Duly licensed insurance companies;
e. Other authorized legal deductions.
